NetBird
  NetBird's client is NetBird's own release archive from its GitHub releases
  (https://github.com/netbirdio/netbird), pinned by size and SHA-256. It is not
  part of this repository or its releases. Installed from TECHO5's add-on
  catalog, the device downloads the archive the catalog pins; installed by hand,
  the add-on downloads it at run time. NetBird's client is BSD-3-Clause
  licensed; its licenses come with the archive and are kept beside the client on
  the device: in the add-on's state folder ($TECHO5_ADDON_STATE/client/LICENSE,
  LICENSES/) from the catalog, in /data/techo5-netbird/client/ by hand.

TECHO5
  Parts are adapted from TECHO5 (https://github.com/HuskerMinion/techo5),
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 TECHO5 contributors: how its built-in NetBird
  ran the client (daemon.go, client.go, the profile edit in profile.go), its
  host name rules (device.go) and firewall check (device.go), and the routes
  from the mesh of HuskerMinion/techo5#603 (routes.go).

